---
import DocsLayout from "../../layouts/docs.astro";
import { ALL_RELEASES_URL, LATEST_RELEASE_URL } from "../../lib/downloads";
---

<DocsLayout title="Installing the app and creator — apprenti.dev Docs">
    <div class="space-y-8">
        <div>
            <h1 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold">
                Installing the app and creator
            </h1>
            <p class="text-muted-foreground mt-2">
                Sideloaded builds from GitHub Releases — there are no
                app-store or Marketplace listings.
            </p>
        </div>

        <div class="prose dark:prose-invert max-w-none space-y-8">
            <section>
                <p class="text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed">
                    Two different products ship in the same release. They
                    are not interchangeable, and the creator is not a
                    second copy of the app.
                </p>
                <ul class="space-y-3 text-muted-foreground mt-4">
                    <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
                        <span class="text-link mt-1">•</span>
                        <span
                            ><strong class="text-foreground">apprenti</strong>
                            — the runtime apprentices and mentors use. It is
                            a desktop or Android app. Pick the archive or
                            APK for your OS.</span
                        >
                    </li>
                    <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
                        <span class="text-link mt-1">•</span>
                        <span
                            ><strong class="text-foreground"
                                >apprenti creator</strong
                            >
                            — a <strong class="text-foreground"
                                >VS Code / Cursor / VSCodium extension</strong
                            >, not an OS installer. You install a
                            <code class="text-sm">.vsix</code> file into the
                            editor. It authors curriculum files; it does not
                            run an apprenticeship or review evidence.</span
                        >
                    </li>
                </ul>
                <p class="text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed mt-4">
                    <a
                        href="/skills"
                        class="text-link hover:underline">AI skill packages</a
                    >
                    are a third thing — editor instruction files for
                    authoring help, not the creator extension and not the
                    app.
                </p>
            </section>

            <nav
                class="rounded-xl border border-border/50 bg-muted/20 px-4 py-3 text-sm"
                aria-label="On this page"
            >
                <p class="font-medium text-foreground mb-2">On this page</p>
                <ul class="flex flex-wrap gap-x-4 gap-y-1 text-muted-foreground">
                    <li>
                        <a href="#download" class="text-link hover:underline"
                            >Download</a
                        >
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <a href="#windows" class="text-link hover:underline"
                            >Windows</a
                        >
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <a href="#macos" class="text-link hover:underline"
                            >macOS</a
                        >
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <a href="#linux" class="text-link hover:underline"
                            >Linux</a
                        >
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <a href="#android" class="text-link hover:underline"
                            >Android</a
                        >
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <a href="#creator" class="text-link hover:underline"
                            >Creator</a
                        >
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <a href="#updates" class="text-link hover:underline"
                            >Updates</a
                        >
                    </li>
                </ul>
            </nav>

            <section id="download" class="scroll-mt-32">
                <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-8 mb-3">
                    Where to download
                </h2>
                <p class="text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed">
                    Every published build lives on the website repository's
                    GitHub Releases — not on Play, App Store, Microsoft
                    Store, or the VS Code Marketplace.
                </p>
                <ul class="space-y-1 text-muted-foreground mt-3">
                    <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
                        <span class="text-link mt-1">•</span>
                        <span
                            ><a
                                href={LATEST_RELEASE_URL}
                                class="text-link hover:underline"
                                target="_blank"
                                rel="noopener noreferrer"
                                >Latest non-prerelease</a
                            >
                            — the newest stable set of files.</span
                        >
                    </li>
                    <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
                        <span class="text-link mt-1">•</span>
                        <span
                            ><a
                                href={ALL_RELEASES_URL}
                                class="text-link hover:underline"
                                target="_blank"
                                rel="noopener noreferrer">All versions</a
                            >
                            — if you need a specific build, including
                            prereleases.</span
                        >
                    </li>
                </ul>
                <p class="text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed mt-4">
                    Filenames include the version. Architecture is in the
                    name too (<code class="text-sm">x64</code> or
                    <code class="text-sm">arm64</code>). Local GGUF model
                    weights are never bundled — you add those later if you
                    want on-device AI.
                </p>
                <ul class="space-y-1 text-muted-foreground mt-3">
                    <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
                        <span class="text-link mt-1">•</span>
                        <span
                            ><code class="text-sm"
                                >apprenti-&lt;version&gt;-windows-&lt;arch&gt;.zip</code
                            >
                            — Windows app</span
                        >
                    </li>
                    <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
                        <span class="text-link mt-1">•</span>
                        <span
                            ><code class="text-sm"
                                >apprenti-&lt;version&gt;-macos-&lt;arch&gt;.zip</code
                            >
                            — macOS app</span
                        >
                    </li>
                    <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
                        <span class="text-link mt-1">•</span>
                        <span
                            ><code class="text-sm"
                                >apprenti-&lt;version&gt;-linux-&lt;arch&gt;.tar.gz</code
                            >
                            — Linux app</span
                        >
                    </li>
                    <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
                        <span class="text-link mt-1">•</span>
                        <span
                            ><code class="text-sm"
                                >apprenti-&lt;version&gt;-android.apk</code
                            >
                            — Android app</span
                        >
                    </li>
                    <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
                        <span class="text-link mt-1">•</span>
                        <span
                            ><code class="text-sm"
                                >apprenti-creator-&lt;version&gt;.vsix</code
                            >
                            — creator extension</span
                        >
                    </li>
                    <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
                        <span class="text-link mt-1">•</span>
                        <span
                            ><code class="text-sm">SHA256SUMS.txt</code> —
                            checksums for the files above</span
                        >
                    </li>
                </ul>
                <p class="text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed mt-4">
                    Desktop builds are unsigned. Windows SmartScreen and
                    macOS Gatekeeper will warn. That is expected for a
                    sideloaded GitHub Release, not a sign the file is
                    damaged.
                </p>
            </section>

            <section id="windows" class="scroll-mt-32">
                <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-8 mb-3">Windows</h2>
                <ol
                    class="space-y-3 text-muted-foreground mt-2 list-decimal pl-5"
                >
                    <li>
                        Download
                        <code class="text-sm"
                            >apprenti-&lt;version&gt;-windows-x64.zip</code
                        >
                        (or <code class="text-sm">arm64</code> if that
                        matches your machine).
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        Unzip the archive to a folder you keep — for
                        example <code class="text-sm">Documents\apprenti</code>.
                        Leave the folder as-is. The
                        <code class="text-sm">.exe</code> needs the DLLs and
                        <code class="text-sm">data</code> directory next to
                        it; do not copy only the executable to the desktop.
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        Run <code class="text-sm">apprenti\apprenti.exe</code>.
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        If SmartScreen says “Windows protected your PC”,
                        choose <strong class="text-foreground">More info</strong>
                        →
                        <strong class="text-foreground">Run anyway</strong>.
                        The build is unsigned; there is no store listing to
                        skip this.
                    </li>
                </ol>
            </section>

            <section id="macos" class="scroll-mt-32">
                <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-8 mb-3">macOS</h2>
                <ol
                    class="space-y-3 text-muted-foreground mt-2 list-decimal pl-5"
                >
                    <li>
                        Download
                        <code class="text-sm"
                            >apprenti-&lt;version&gt;-macos-arm64.zip</code
                        >
                        on Apple silicon, or
                        <code class="text-sm">…-macos-x64.zip</code> on
                        Intel.
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        Double-click the zip to unpack
                        <code class="text-sm">apprenti.app</code>. Drag it
                        to <strong class="text-foreground">Applications</strong>
                        if you want it on the Launchpad, or run it from the
                        unzipped folder.
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        Do not double-click to launch the first time.
                        Control-click (or right-click)
                        <code class="text-sm">apprenti.app</code> →
                        <strong class="text-foreground">Open</strong> →
                        <strong class="text-foreground">Open</strong> again
                        in the dialog. Gatekeeper blocks unsigned apps on a
                        normal double-click.
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        If macOS still refuses, open
                        <strong class="text-foreground"
                            >System Settings → Privacy &amp; Security</strong
                        >
                        and choose
                        <strong class="text-foreground">Open Anyway</strong>
                        for apprenti.
                    </li>
                </ol>
            </section>

            <section id="linux" class="scroll-mt-32">
                <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-8 mb-3">Linux</h2>
                <ol
                    class="space-y-3 text-muted-foreground mt-2 list-decimal pl-5"
                >
                    <li>
                        Download
                        <code class="text-sm"
                            >apprenti-&lt;version&gt;-linux-x64.tar.gz</code
                        >
                        (or <code class="text-sm">arm64</code>).
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        Extract the tarball. You should get an
                        <code class="text-sm">apprenti/</code> directory
                        with the binary at
                        <code class="text-sm">apprenti/apprenti</code>.
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        From a terminal:
                        <pre
                            class="mt-2 rounded-lg border border-border/50 bg-muted/30 p-3 text-sm overflow-x-auto"
                        ><code>chmod +x apprenti/apprenti
./apprenti/apprenti</code></pre>
                    </li>
                </ol>
                <p class="text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed mt-4">
                    This is a portable Flutter bundle, not a
                    <code class="text-sm">.deb</code> or AppImage. It
                    expects a desktop Linux with GTK 3. If the binary exits
                    immediately, <code class="text-sm">ldd apprenti/apprenti</code>
                    will show any missing shared libraries.
                </p>
            </section>

            <section id="android" class="scroll-mt-32">
                <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-8 mb-3">Android</h2>
                <ol
                    class="space-y-3 text-muted-foreground mt-2 list-decimal pl-5"
                >
                    <li>
                        Download
                        <code class="text-sm"
                            >apprenti-&lt;version&gt;-android.apk</code
                        >
                        on the phone (or copy it over).
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        Open the APK from Files or the browser. Android
                        will ask you to allow that app to
                        <strong class="text-foreground"
                            >install unknown apps</strong
                        >
                        — enable it for the Files app or browser you used,
                        then confirm the install.
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        Open <strong class="text-foreground">apprenti</strong>
                        from the launcher.
                    </li>
                </ol>
                <p class="text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed mt-4">
                    Current APKs are signed with the debug key until a
                    release keystore is configured. Installing a later
                    store-signed or keystore-signed build over this one
                    will fail — uninstall the debug-signed app first
                    (that wipes local app data on the device; your
                    curriculum Git repository on disk or remote is
                    separate).
                </p>
            </section>

            <section id="creator" class="scroll-mt-32">
                <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-8 mb-3">
                    Installing apprenti creator
                </h2>
                <p class="text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed">
                    Creator is only an editor extension. Mentors and
                    apprentices who are not authoring a curriculum do not
                    need it. Authors still install the
                    <strong class="text-foreground">app</strong> separately
                    if they want to walk the path as an apprentice or
                    review as a mentor.
                </p>
                <p class="text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed mt-4">
                    You need
                    <a
                        href="https://code.visualstudio.com/"
                        class="text-link hover:underline"
                        target="_blank"
                        rel="noopener noreferrer">VS Code</a
                    >
                    1.85+,
                    <a
                        href="https://cursor.com/"
                        class="text-link hover:underline"
                        target="_blank"
                        rel="noopener noreferrer">Cursor</a
                    >, or
                    <a
                        href="https://vscodium.com/"
                        class="text-link hover:underline"
                        target="_blank"
                        rel="noopener noreferrer">VSCodium</a
                    >.
                </p>
                <ol
                    class="space-y-3 text-muted-foreground mt-4 list-decimal pl-5"
                >
                    <li>
                        Download
                        <code class="text-sm"
                            >apprenti-creator-&lt;version&gt;.vsix</code
                        >
                        from the same GitHub Release as the app.
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        In the editor: open the Extensions view → the
                        <strong class="text-foreground">…</strong> menu
                        (Views and More Actions) →
                        <strong class="text-foreground"
                            >Install from VSIX…</strong
                        >
                        → pick that file. Reload if asked.
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <strong class="text-foreground">File → Open Folder</strong>
                        on a curriculum working copy — a folder that
                        contains <code class="text-sm">curriculum.json</code>
                        or <code class="text-sm">curricula.json</code>.
                        Creator stays dormant on a folder that is only the
                        Flutter app repo or a random project.
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        Confirm the
                        <strong class="text-foreground">Creator</strong>
                        icon on the activity bar. The Curricula view should
                        list the path in that folder.
                    </li>
                </ol>
                <p class="text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed mt-4">
                    From a terminal, with the editor's CLI on
                    <code class="text-sm">PATH</code>:
                </p>
                <pre
                    class="mt-2 rounded-lg border border-border/50 bg-muted/30 p-3 text-sm overflow-x-auto"
                ><code>code --install-extension ./apprenti-creator-0.1.0.vsix
# or: cursor --install-extension ./apprenti-creator-0.1.0.vsix
# or: codium --install-extension ./apprenti-creator-0.1.0.vsix</code></pre>
                <p class="text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed mt-4">
                    Uninstall from the Extensions view, or
                    <code class="text-sm"
                        >code --uninstall-extension apprenti-dev.apprenti-creator</code
                    >.
                </p>
                <p class="text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed mt-4">
                    After it is installed,
                    <a
                        href="/docs/creator-authoring-with-apprenti-creator"
                        class="text-link hover:underline"
                        >Authoring with apprenti creator</a
                    >
                    covers the Path canvas, editors, and validation.
                    Creator writes files; it does not wrap Git — commit
                    and push from the editor's ordinary source-control
                    view.
                </p>
            </section>

            <section id="updates" class="scroll-mt-32">
                <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-8 mb-3">
                    Updates and checksums
                </h2>
                <p class="text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed">
                    There is no in-app updater. Download the new release
                    and replace the previous install: unzip Windows/macOS
                    over the old folder (or drop a new
                    <code class="text-sm">.app</code> in Applications),
                    extract a new Linux tarball, install a new Android APK
                    over the existing one (same signing key), or install
                    the new VSIX over the old extension.
                </p>
                <p class="text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed mt-4">
                    Each release includes
                    <code class="text-sm">SHA256SUMS.txt</code>. To check a
                    downloaded file:
                </p>
                <pre
                    class="mt-2 rounded-lg border border-border/50 bg-muted/30 p-3 text-sm overflow-x-auto"
                ><code># Windows (PowerShell)
Get-FileHash .\apprenti-0.1.0-windows-x64.zip -Algorithm SHA256

# macOS / Linux
shasum -a 256 apprenti-0.1.0-macos-arm64.zip</code></pre>
                <p class="text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed mt-4">
                    The digest should match the line for that filename in
                    <code class="text-sm">SHA256SUMS.txt</code>.
                </p>
            </section>

            <section>
                <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-8 mb-3">Next</h2>
                <p class="text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed">
                    With the app installed,
                    <a
                        href="/docs/apprentice-getting-started"
                        class="text-link hover:underline">Getting started</a
                    >
                    covers opening a curriculum. Mentors continue with
                    <a
                        href="/docs/mentor-setting-up-repository"
                        class="text-link hover:underline"
                        >Setting up a curriculum repository</a
                    >.
                </p>
            </section>
        </div>

        <div class="mt-8 flex gap-4">
            <a href="/docs" class="text-sm text-link hover:underline"
                >← All Docs</a
            >
            <a href="/" class="text-sm text-muted-foreground hover:underline"
                >Back to apprenti.dev</a
            >
        </div>
    </div>
</DocsLayout>
